omxplorer, a desktop data app (1440x900), its Start screen. A floating slim menu bar at the top (File, Edit, View, Insert, Data, Format, Help). Left: a floating panel 280px wide with the app name "omxplorer" and actions as rows with icons: New blank sheet, Open file…, Settings…; at its bottom a small card "GPU · RTX 4090 ready" with a green dot and the line "Parquet files bigger than memory open too: streamed from disk." Main area: a large rounded drop zone "Drop a CSV, Parquet or .omx file here" with an upload icon, a line "A million rows is fine: you see a preview first", and a "Choose a file" primary pill button. Below: "Recent" as a clean list of 4 files (icon, name, path in small grey, opened time, an Open button on hover). Then "Try a sample": three equal cards: Orders (1M rows · a year of sales), Blank sheet (an empty table to type into), Taxi trips (100M rows · a GPU workout). Bottom status strip: "Ready" and "omxplorer · omxapp".
